## 6. Debugging History & Failure Modes

Confidence: ✅ High — recently verified in this session.

- The mandated automation guard command’s trailing `.` was rejected as an unsupported argument;
  the exact supported command without it returned `decision=allow`.
- Vitest initially collected Playwright specs; `vitest.config.ts` now limits it to unit tests.
- TypeScript initially lacked Node and PDF declarations; `@types/node` plus the package’s typed
  PDF entry resolved the issue.
- Current advisories affected initial dependency resolutions; locked patched versions and
  transitive overrides reduced `npm audit` to zero vulnerabilities.
- Screenshot inspection found low readability in one emulated hover state; explicit
  `--surface-hover` tokens fixed it and the new hover axe/screenshot proof passed.
- The local Vite process ended between Browser captures; the in-app Browser then stayed on its
  connection-error page and policy-blocked localhost. Playwright was the allowed fallback.
- Expected input failures are missing/multiple proposal candidates, no readable addendum IDs,
  unsupported types, image-only PDF text absence, and file size/count bounds.

