## 8. Risks, Technical Debt & Strict Preservation Rules

Confidence: ✅ High — recently verified in this session.

Risks:

- Users may overread `ACKNOWLEDGED` as legal bid responsiveness despite the limitation.
- Source snippets can contain sensitive bid content in the local result/download.
- Proposal scoring is deliberately narrow and will stop on ambiguous final-file sets.

Do Not Touch without explicit instruction:

- Do not weaken the visible-evidence/legal-responsiveness limitation.
- Do not upgrade generic “all addenda” language to exact evidence.
- Do not add uploads, accounts, credentials, providers, payments, telemetry, or hosted storage to
  the core path.
- Do not remove input bounds or safe text-node rendering.
- Do not add a selector, secondary page, settings, theme control, or extra dominant action.
- Do not call public pain evidence demand, buyer, usage, payment, revenue, or product-market-fit
  proof.
- Do not deploy GitHub Pages or any application infrastructure.

